# Vue/Nuxt Frontend Patterns

## Component Structure

Prefer Composition API with `<script setup>` syntax. Use TypeScript for type safety.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'

interface AbsencePeriod {
  start_date: string
  end_date: string
}

const periods = ref<AbsencePeriod[]>([])
const isLoading = ref(false)
</script>

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<script>
export default {
  data() {
    return { periods: [] }
  }
}
</script>
```

## State Management

- Use Pinia for complex shared state
- Use composables for reusable logic (e.g., `useAbsenceCalculator.ts`)
- Keep component state local when possible

## WASM Integration

Load WASM module on app initialization. Expose calculation functions through composables.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - composable pattern
export const useAbsenceCalculator = () => {
  const calculate = async (periods: AbsencePeriod[]) => {
    const wasm = await import('@/wasm/ilr_calculator')
    return wasm.calculate_rolling_absences(JSON.stringify(periods))
  }
  return { calculate }
}
```

## File Organization

```
components/
  ui/          # shadcn/ui components
  AbsenceForm.vue
composables/
  useAbsenceCalculator.ts
types/
  absence.ts
wasm/
  ilr_calculator_bg.wasm
```

## Error Handling

Handle WASM errors gracefully. Show user-friendly error messages.

```typescript
try {
  const result = await calculateAbsences(periods)
} catch (error) {
  // Show user-friendly error message
  errorMessage.value = 'Failed to calculate absences. Please check your input.'
}
```

## Performance

- Lazy load WASM module
- Use `v-memo` for expensive list rendering
- Debounce user input for calculations

## Mobile-First Design

Design components for mobile screens first, then enhance for larger screens.

- Use mobile-optimized layouts (single column, full-width inputs)
- Ensure touch targets are at least 44x44px
- Optimize for portrait orientation (primary use case)
- Use mobile-friendly form inputs (date pickers, touch keyboards)
- Consider mobile performance (minimize re-renders, optimize WASM loading)

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD - Mobile-first layout -->
<template>
  <div class="w-full px-4 py-6 space-y-4">
    <Input class="w-full" v-model="date" />
    <Button class="w-full sm:w-auto">Calculate</Button>
  </div>
</template>

<!-- ❌ BAD - Desktop-first layout -->
<template>
  <div class="flex gap-4">
    <Input class="w-64" />
    <Button>Calculate</Button>
  </div>
</template>
```
